+# Live Broadcom research record
+
+Accessed 2026-08-14. These were real network reads used to check the pinned
+architecture. The compatibility snapshot remains the reproducible build input.
+
+- https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/425164/vcenter-upgrade-precheck-from-version-8x.html
+  — Broadcom documents that the NSX 4.2.2.1 / vCenter 9.x combination is an
+  SDDC Manager-managed upgrade scenario, not a greenfield combination, and that
+  an out-of-VCF NSX 4.x deployment must be imported before its 9.x upgrade.
+- https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article?articleNumber=404155 —
+  Broadcom documents centralized 9.x entitlement through VCF Operations and
+  convergence of an existing vCenter through VCF Installer.
+- https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/408127/steps-to-converge-to-vmware-live-recover.html
+  — Broadcom documents the 9.0.2.2-or-later prerequisite and the supported
+  fresh-9.0.4-deploy plus converge/configuration-migration path for the formerly
+  separate Live Site Recovery and vSphere Replication appliances.
+- https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/444864/vcf-protection-and-recovery-91-transitio.html
+  — Broadcom documents the unified VCF Protection and Recovery 9.1 target,
+  deprecation of separate SRM/VR appliances at 9.1, and the usual transition
+  through the unified 9.0.4 appliance.
+
+No observed live statement conflicted with the facts used from the pinned
+snapshot for this estate.
